    "created_at": "2021-05-20T15:44:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-05-20T15:44:16Z",
    "body": "My understanding is that Google and Apple are happy to not formally object to CSS Ruby being worked on by its editors, but they have not made any movement to implement it.\r\n\r\nI think the framing in @murata2makoto's comment is needlessly inflammatory. There are at least three versions of the web platform: those implemented by WebKit, Gecko, and Blink respectively. They are not always in sync. And there are different specs covering different aspects of them.\r\n\r\nRight now, and for the foreseeable future, the Gecko version of the web platform supports CSS Ruby and rb/rtc. The WebKit/Blink version does not. This is similar to how the Blink version of the web platform supports Web Serial, and the WebKit/Gecko versions do not. This is OK, and happens all the time. It's how we move the web forward.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/845234165/reactions",
